            "ev:a03fb3775b2558fa37682815d8eca882312c7f19d5753c2fac95aa48bc930cfb"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "NINDS describes Parkinson’s disease as a progressive nervous-system disorder involving nerve-cell damage and death; WHO also describes worsening over time. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/parkinsons-disease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:71bde977b2f16129472d1872098e0a9407018fb99d56410053660ad1f5ed06e6",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3b15eb21c764088160abfa6fe4a9e5f9d47e04d440f2e70015a54de89bfc0695",
            "ev:c4408a793411bb86479a03ab7b81c6716e7081d0ffa331b661597cfff9d1c890"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/parkinson-disease"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson’s Foundation distinguishes parkinsonism, a set of movement symptoms, from a specific diagnosis; the MDS criteria separately assess whether Parkinson’s disease is its cause. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/understanding-parkinsons/what-is-parkinsons/types-parkinsonisms",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b730f9b318e2ac2a498ad2b2fe3e6b08ed42a47a9dd384990bc6ed87d0504195",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:681b596446d5cc1a1a37e3c0e1f4bf0449d57b06c365ddf3a532c9c9e6eab21d",
            "ev:e5f5016222c43ea813af859f2ebf9421e1cefd3023bfb5bf94e8f3ba1068a407"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26474316/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For determining Parkinson’s disease as the cause of parkinsonism, the MDS criteria use absolute exclusions, red flags counterbalanced by supportive criteria, and supportive features. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26474316/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:87906b709aef552d24139ae5a0502ba9e1b7c6fd62e6531c4f0eb48054bbbf2a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a3aaf9ac1382bcb58fbcf939a7e3c75da7851f916b60ad691fa20bb24aed8064"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The MDS criteria distinguish clinically established Parkinson’s disease, prioritizing specificity, from probable disease, balancing sensitivity and specificity. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26474316/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dbb0e1773a3845e14c799f427dea2d01a1dea32e13a9db4a643765d7011d12a3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:33c5a057bf84df4d1754e775991cb4d7f7cf12cc71e8b16b25d44dc47e909356"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "WHO and NINDS describe non-motor involvement in Parkinson’s disease, including mental-health and sleep problems. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/parkinson-disease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1c5904111848843a60de05e3cb19fdbbd1e8391a0d5bd66f545b41c926495295",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9fda6f170fd885b99da67f130bbae230c3e738ffbabc389ad7d8dc84e8c6fcf0",
            "ev:e2df4f1e38eff92d172bf4686bea394ba792f668f2eec1df92b8245d6fc6dc7d",
            "ev:e341a495c98d2bc84af909103df5c87ae84d88773bf88149a60b83e886d5c4dc"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/parkinsons-disease",
            "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/parkinsons-disease"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NINDS notes that some people with Parkinson’s disease never develop tremor. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/parkinsons-disease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1b86ea552dc0c5dd298c159167cbf5772ee1e31316b1dd920001429ff9307a79",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9f75a1506aa21bbedcacae76ba587f83d820dba7d5bcf60992c33c3d1c3ec6c5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NINDS states that no specific single test can definitively diagnose Parkinson’s disease. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/parkinsons-disease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:98df6ed74ddca18e7e7fd1d6a466928070bd658daa379a3e7e3d7feebde19440",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0d9184b0fa4cb8c1f22cecabef4f50ee4794a0e8cb57f4e901b77fc1479b9a1b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NINDS states that a dopamine transporter scan cannot distinguish Parkinson’s disease from atypical parkinsonism; Beach and Adler likewise describe dopamine functional scans as lacking specificity for Parkinson’s disease. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/parkinsons-disease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f40b0547aaaee1421c9d1a43921acd262f4d47647d039a23b434cff3a61e99c2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:230d288cb730f8371b05a544fd172434494e5e37d6db8a9b08a8d375b10b91e4",
            "ev:5567235745f4ce4f7b180aa546807310c5d9c933cfb0bfeaa94dba0a29d0c25c"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6544441/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "WHO reported that global estimates for 2019 showed over 8.5 million individuals with Parkinson’s disease. (low confidence) (verified as of 2023-08-09)",
          "source": "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/parkinson-disease",
