      "documentConcept": "Movement disorders and neurodegeneration landscape",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:584736ab4b61b1128717907c2e797510857e645eddda817b0da1d16b83b4860a",
      "text": "Parkinson’s disease is a progressive nervous-system disorder with movement and non-motor manifestations. Parkinsonism describes a movement syndrome rather than a specific diagnosis, and secondary causes broaden its differential diagnosis. The MDS clinical criteria formalize syndrome recognition and assessment of Parkinson’s disease as its cause. Clinical uncertainty, including the limitations of dopamine imaging and early diagnosis, remains central to interpreting the landscape. WHO also documents a substantial global burden and unequal access to care.",
